                "endLine": 174,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t * A starting bounce buffer is needed if the alignment of file_offs\n\t * and buf_offs within their respective pages do not match.\n\t * This means the data from file_offs cannot be directly written\n\t * starting at buf_offs without requiring a shift or overwriting\n\t * data before buf_offs within the same page.\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 175,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 176,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tif ((file_offs \u0026 (PAGE_SIZE - 1)) !\u003d (buf_offs \u0026 (PAGE_SIZE - 1))) {\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 177,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 181,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t\t * The first PAGE_SIZE of data read from the file (starting at\n\t\t * PAGE_ALIGN_DOWN(file_offs)) must go into a bounce buffer.\n\t\t * The direct I/O to the destination buffer will start at the\n\t\t * first page boundary *after* the portion that would be covered\n\t\t * by the data copied from the bounce buffer.\n\t\t * The data copied from the bounce buffer covers up to:\n\t\t * buf_offs + (PAGE_SIZE - offset_in_page(file_offs))\n\t\t * The direct read into the destination buffer can start at the\n\t\t * next page boundary.\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "drivers/android/wrapfd.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 185,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 186,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\t} else\n\t\tdirect_read_start_offs \u003d buf_offs;\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
